{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "John in Peru", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "An Amazing Civilization", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 15, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "medic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a first aid officer", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You need to call a medic if you are in an accident.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use on a trip.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "temple", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a building of worship", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's hard work to build temples with stone!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to head down", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to head for or move forwards.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We need to head down the hill.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ruin", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the pieces of a building that was destroyed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The city was in ruins.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "spectacular", "type": "name"}, {"content": "wonderful, very impressive", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The scenery was spectacular.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "others", "type": "name"}, {"content": "additional people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The others had to leave at five o'clock.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "nauseous", "type": "name"}, {"content": "feeling sick", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I am starting to feel nauseous.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dizzy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a feeling that you are turning around in circles", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm spinning so fast that I'm feeling dizzy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob04aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Pronouncing the word The", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You pronounce the word \u201cthe\u201d in different ways.<br> It is often pronounced \u201cthee\u201d before a vowel sound and \u201cthuh\u201d before a consonant sound.<br>The sound differences help with the flow of speech.<br>  <br><span class=\"italic\">Example: \u201cthee\u201d air vs. \u201cthe\u201d scenery</span><br>  <br>When used for <span class=\"strong\">emphasis</span>, <span class=\"italic\">the</span> is always pronounced <span class=\"strong\">\"thee\"</span> never \"thuh\".<br>  <br>It is the <span class=\"strong\">sound</span> that is important, not the letter you use in writing a word.  You use a long \"thee\" before a <span class=\"strong\">vowel sound</span>,  not always before a vowel.<br>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You write\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"With\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You say\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reason\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">the house</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"consonant h\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thuh <span class=\\\"strong\\\">h</span>ouse\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"consonant sound\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">the</span> hour\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"consonant h\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thee <span class=\\\"strong\\\">o</span>ur\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"vowel sound\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">the university</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"vowel u\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thuh <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> y</span>ouniversity\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"consonant sound\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">the umbrella</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"vowel u\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thee <span class=\\\"strong\\\">u</span>mbrella\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"vowel sound\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Showing Interest and Surprise", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use these phrases and techniques to show interest and surprise in conversation:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: These are the ruins.<br><span class=\"strong\">Tourist</span>: Oh, really? How interesting!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Showing Interest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Showing Surprise\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Oh?<br> Oh, yeah?<br> Really?<br> Oh, really?<br> Is that right?<br> How fascinating/interesting!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Wow!<br>Spectacular!</br> Amazing!<br> Get out of here!<br> Unbelievable!<br> No!\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write 8-10 lines of 